is_expandable': True, 'note_tweet_results': {'result': {'id': 'Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjE4NzYzNTYyNzU1MzkyNTEyMDA=', 'text': "How is handedness analogous to gender ideology? Whatever the facts about handedness and its genetic determinants, these facts have no discernible bearing on the fact that gender is binary and immutable. \n\nIf the analogy is about suppression of certain handedness, then it's truly a terrible analogy, since gender in nature is not a matter of cultural or societal suppression. \n\nHaving spent my summers on a farm, I can attest to the fact that none of the animals were this or that gender because my grandfather and great-grandfather forced them to be what they were. They were this or that gender just because they were—and there were always only two (and they often needed to be separated).\n\nIt's not more complicated than this. Gender ideology is the complicating force because its advocates seek certain ends, namely the production of confused children for profit, status, and other more lurid ends.", 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': []}, 'richtext': {'richtext_tags': []}, 'media': {'inline_media': []}}}}, 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 1, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Mon Jan 06 19:52:51 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1876026685377634676', 'display_text_range': [14, 293], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '69156861', 'name': 'Chief Nerd', 'screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'indices': [0, 13]}]}, 'favorite_count': 1, 'favorited': False, 'full_text': "@TheChiefNerd How is handedness analogous to gender ideology? Whatever the facts about handedness and its genetic determinants, these facts have no discernible bearing on the fact that gender is binary and immutable. \n\nIf the analogy is about suppression of certain handedness, then it's truly", 'in_reply_to_screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'in_reply_to_status_id_str': '1876026685377634676', 'in_re